From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <acholleti@qti.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifiGen_fsm: disable FH on MLO neighbour radio in s_syncOnEpStartConnFail

In s_syncOnEpStartConnFail(), when a bSTA connect fails with -EBUSY,
s_disableFronthaul() is called on pRad to release radio control to
wpa_supplicant.  In MLO configurations the last distinct neighbour
radio in the MLD link set may also need to be disabled.

Iterate the MLD neighbour links to find the last distinct neighbour
radio (pNgRad, hoisted outside the loop for post-loop use):
  - if no distinct neighbour found (NULL or same as pRad): disable pRad.
  - otherwise: disable pNgRad.

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <acholleti@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c
@@ -1999,7 +1999,27 @@
         SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: disable fronthaul to allow wpa_supplicant to connect on chspec %s to %s",
                            pEP->Name, swl_typeChanspecExt_toBuf32(chanSpec).buf,
                            swl_typeMacBin_toBuf32Ref(bssid).buf);
-        s_disableFronthaul(pRad);
+        /* Also disable fronthaul on each MLO neighbour radio so none of them
+         * block the wpa_supplicant connection attempt on this radio. */
+        T_SSID* pSSID = pEP->pSSID;
+        T_Radio* pNgRad = NULL;
+        if(pSSID && pSSID->pMldLink) {
+            wld_for_eachNeighMldLink_safe(pNgLink, pSSID->pMldLink) {
+                T_SSID* pNgSSID = wld_mld_getLinkSsid(pNgLink);
+                if(!pNgSSID || (pNgSSID == pSSID)) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+                pNgRad = pNgSSID->RADIO_PARENT;
+                if(!pNgRad || (pNgRad == pRad)) {
+                    continue;
+                }
+            }
+        }
+        if(!pNgRad || (pNgRad == pRad)) {
+            s_disableFronthaul(pRad);
+        } else {
+            s_disableFronthaul(pNgRad);
+        }
     }
 }
 
